    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0496" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg408"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Philip to M. Malmusi.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>:</p>
                <p>In pursuance of your letter to the consul-general of June 13 last, I have the
                    honor to inform you that I am in receipt of instructions from my Government
                    authorizing me to enter into a reciprocal agreement with the Government of the
                    Kingdom of Italy and the United States, the agreement to be for the mutual
                    protection of trade-marks registered in Italy and the United States against
                    infringement in Morocco by subjects of the respective nations, on the lines of
                    that now existing between the United States and Great Britain.</p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Minister, the assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hoffman Philip</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Acting Consul-General.</hi></item>
                            <item>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Malmusi</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Minister of Italy.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
